# SSH host keys for the lawrider.uk box (lawrider-uk, europe-west2-a).
#
# Checked into the repository on purpose. These are PUBLIC keys, so there is
# nothing here to keep secret — and putting them in version control buys the one
# property a secret does not: changing them takes a pull request that somebody
# reads. A secret can be rewritten silently by anyone with write access, which
# is exactly the actor this file exists to stop.
#
# Before this, every workflow ran `ssh-keyscan` and trusted whatever answered,
# on every run. That is trust-on-first-use with the "first" removed: not a
# weaker check than pinning, but no check at all, in jobs that hold a key which
# can write to production.
#
# Captured 2026-09-20 from three independent sources that agreed byte for byte:
#   - /etc/ssh/ssh_host_*_key.pub read off the box over an already-authenticated
#     session, which is the strongest attestation available
#   - ssh-keyscan from the network
#   - the known_hosts entry established when the box was first provisioned
#
#   ED25519  SHA256:CEhHqmzA95UMcb+XiniNG4CPC+qfIwrWXIwLkftleVI
#   RSA      SHA256:0LcjCrq9cgowE0qY/1Uq4zwDo+2KyXEaJ8krX6Bw43M
#   ECDSA    SHA256:wBLjBqao5HoZyN/PHwd912gkNDZ2e37lKRKDfGQe3hQ
#
# ⚠ Rebuilding the box generates new keys and every job that uses this file will
# refuse to connect until it is updated — deliberately. provision-lawrider-uk.yml
# (in overthelex/lawrider-uk)
# prints the new keys at the end for exactly that.
